# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo when a release is archived.
# Tag the GitHub release v5 so the Zenodo record matches the version below.
# Before the first public release: check author names and add ORCID iDs.
# After the Zenodo DOI is issued: add the two lines
#   doi: "10.5281/zenodo.NNNNNNN"
#   date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Raman peak extractor for graphene nanoribbon spectra"
version: "5"
abstract: >-
  Browser-based program for baseline subtraction, Si calibration and
  constrained multi-Lorentzian fitting of Raman spectra of graphene
  nanoribbons, with uncertainties estimated by a Monte Carlo of the
  full analysis.
authors:
